{"flags":[{"id":"1970s-nasa-graphics-manual","tags":["fact","incoherent"],"problems":["family: the rewrite still says 'postmodern and 1980s', so the earlier problem is unchanged.","family: the mid 1970s NASA Graphics Standards Manual is late modernist, Swiss-derived work, and this label groups it with Memphis and 1980s directions that contradict its strict grid and spec-caption idea."],"fix":"Change family to 'mid-century and space age', which fits the 1970s late modernist space program work. Leave the rest of the card as written."},{"id":"asiri-escarpment-switchbacks","tags":["generic","region"],"problems":["name: the rewrite renamed the card 'Hairpin Switchbacks' and dropped the Asir place word, but region is still 'gulf'.","palette and texture: night asphalt, painted line white, reflector amber and road-paint bead speckle belong to any mountain road. Swap Asir for the Alps and the card reads the same, which was the earlier problem.","nameAr: 'منعطفات العقبة' points to a Saudi mountain pass, but nothing in the English name, imagery or palette carries that place."],"fix":"Pick one direction. Either keep it as a generic layout rule and set region to 'global' with a neutral nameAr, or restore the Asir escarpment with one or two real local moves, such as the color of the escarpment rock in the support slot and a crop of the real Asir pass roads, without inventing facts."}]}
```

