{"flags":[{"id":"debossed-leather","tags":["incoherent"],"problems":["family: still 'soft, rubber or inflatable', the exact problem raised before. Tanned saddle leather is a hide, not rubber or an inflatable.","family: the wrong family will still group this card with balloons and rubber when the tool bends a page, which breaks the leather system the rest of the card builds."],"fix":"Move the card to 'textile and fiber', the closest material family for hide and stitched leather goods, and leave the rest of the card as it is."},{"id":"every-word-hand-lettered","tags":["incoherent","weak-copy"],"problems":["idea: says the main call to action is written in thick marker, but avoid bans the marker face on buttons and on anything under 20 px, so the card contradicts itself on its key element.","name: 'Every Word Hand-Lettered' no longer matches the rule, which now limits marker to headings and one action while labels, buttons and reading text stay in a sans.","surprise: 'one marker-written headline per view' disagrees with the idea, which puts marker on all headings plus the call to action."],"fix":"Pick one rule and use it in every field. For example, allow only one marker headline per view and keep every button in Work Sans, or allow a single large marker CTA of 20 px or more and say so in avoid. Then rename the card to match, for example 'Hand-Lettered Headlines'."},{"id":"game-cartridge","tags":["incoherent"],"problems":["family: still 'dial, panel or machine', the exact problem raised before, while 'game, toy or sport gear' fits the object directly.","family: the shell, label and collectible shelf ideas describe a game piece you hold and collect, so filing the card under control panels still misfiles it."],"fix":"Set family to 'game, toy or sport gear' and leave the rest of the card as it is."}]}
```

